%SIXMD 1
# @?OBJDUMP - INSPECT A DOBJ OBJECT

## DESCRIPTION

OBJDUMP INSPECTS A DOBJ1 RELOCATABLE OBJECT. IT CAN PRINT THE OBJECT HEADER,
GLOBAL SYMBOLS, RELOCATIONS, AND A PDP-6/PDP-10 TEXT DISASSEMBLY.

USAGE IS 'OBJDUMP [-H] [-T] [-R] [-D] OBJECT.DOBJ'.

WITH NO DISPLAY OPTION, ALL FOUR VIEWS ARE PRINTED.

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-H
PRINT THE DOBJ SECTION/SYMBOL/RELOCATION COUNTS. THIS IS AN OBJDUMP HEADER
OPTION; DAIMOS DOES NOT RESERVE -H AS A GENERAL HELP OPTION.

### @?-T
PRINT THE SYMBOL TABLE.

### @?-R
PRINT RELOCATION RECORDS.

### @?-D
DISASSEMBLE THE TEXT SECTION.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?OBJECT.DOBJ
DOBJ1 OBJECT TO INSPECT.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - OBJECT INSPECTED
### @?1 - INVALID OBJECT OR OUTPUT ERROR

